{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He saw the crowds and climbed the moun[C]tain, sat down on the [G]ground
His followers came close to [C]him, the people gathered [G]round
He looked upon the weary ones, [C]the poor and the op[G]pressed
[D]And he began to teach them, [C]saying who is [D]truly [G]blessed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs [C]is the kingdom of [G]heaven
Blessed are those who mourn, for they [C]will be [D]comforted
[Em]Blessed are the meek, for they [D]will inherit the [G]earth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The widow at the grave[C]side and the farmer in the [G]drought
